  if(name==='Return to the 1960 Constitutional Order'){var common='Cyprus will remain one independent republic under a revised 1960 constitutional order. Territorial autonomy has been set aside, and the agreements reached on representation, administration, security, courts, guarantees and troops will define the Turkish community’s future.';return common+'\n\n'+(Q.cyprus_constitution_result==='turkish'?'What a diplomatic victory! Our delegation has carried the strength won on the battlefield into the heart of the state. Turkish rights now rest on powerful constitutional safeguards, and the community has a voice that cannot simply be brushed aside. With every Turkish proposal accepted, this achievement can stand above even a territorial settlement: our people remain throughout Cyprus, protected by the very institutions that once failed them. Ankara returns with its head held high!':Q.cyprus_constitution_result==='greek'?'This is a bitter settlement. Too many of our demands have been surrendered, and the government cannot dress those concessions as a triumph. The reassurance is that Turkish Cypriots are no longer under immediate threat and Turkey has avoided international damage. We have secured peace, but the result feels painfully close to defeat.':'There is relief, but little cause for celebration. We did not obtain the lasting position we sought, and several hard-won demands have become compromises. Still, the new safeguards offer a chance for peaceful coexistence. Our task now is to make those promises work.');}
